CRASH-23: reject node index 0 in EN_setlinknodes

EN_setlinknodes tested its node arguments with "< 0", so node index 0
was accepted and a link could be attached to the unused slot Node[0].
The connectivity check that runs after a hydraulic warning then counts
node 0 as an extra node and writes past the end of its node list
(report.c, disconnected() and marknodes()). Test "<= 0", as the link
index check above does.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-23_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..9be0a04 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -3834,8 +3834,8 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinknodes(EN_Project p, int index, int node1, int node2)
     if (index <= 0 || index > net->Nlinks) return 204;
 
     // Check that nodes exist
-    if (node1 < 0 || node1 > net->Nnodes) return 203;
-    if (node2 < 0 || node2 > net->Nnodes) return 203;
+    if (node1 <= 0 || node1 > net->Nnodes) return 203;
+    if (node2 <= 0 || node2 > net->Nnodes) return 203;
 
     // Check that nodes are not the same
     if (node1 == node2) return 222;
